# TuneTalez

Vertical short-episode drama app (1–3 min episodes, swipe-to-watch) for a mobile-first Indian audience. Monetized later by per-episode coin unlocks (Phase 3). Progress and list state sync across web, iOS, and Android on one account. Target scale: 10,000 users.

Core journey (Phase 1): open Home → browse series rails → open a series → sign in with email OTP → save to My List → sign out. Episode video player, paywall, and coin purchase land in later phases.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
| --- | --- |
| App | Expo SDK + Expo Router, TypeScript (iOS, Android, Web) |
| State / data | Direct Supabase client calls in Phase 1 (no Zustand / TanStack Query yet) |
| Auth / DB | Supabase (Postgres, RLS, email OTP) |
| Static / posters | Cloudflare R2 + custom domains |
| Web hosting | Cloudflare Pages |
| Mobile release | EAS Build + EAS Submit + EAS Update (later phases) |
| Payments | Phase 3 only — see `payments.mdc` |

Phase 1 talks to staging Supabase and staging R2/Pages only. No payment SDKs, tables, or accounts in Phase 1.

## Guardrails

- State assumptions before writing code. If two interpretations exist, ask rather than pick silently.
- Minimum code for the task. No abstractions, config options, or error handling for scenarios that can't happen.
- One roadmap phase per prompt, with a stated success check.
- Touch only the files a step needs. Don't improve unrelated code.
- Keep a plain-English `TASKS.md` so a non-technical builder can track what's done without reading code.
- One repo, two environments (`staging` / `production` branches). Secrets live only in each platform's secret store — never in a committed `.env`.
- No caching layer, queue, or Redis at this scale. Revisit only past roughly 50k DAU or if heavy real-time features are added.
- Never touch production Supabase, the old R2 bucket, or `cdn.tunetalez.com` from Phase 1 work.

## Roadmap

1. Foundation — Supabase schema + RLS, email OTP auth, Home / Series / My List / Profile, staging Pages + R2 posters
2. Content & Video — episode player, free/paywall logic, Stream (or equivalent) upload pipeline
3. Payments — coin wallet + purchases per `payments.mdc` (Razorpay web, Apple IAP iOS, Play Billing Android)
4. Polish & Store Prep — EAS builds, app store assets, QA across web/iOS/Android
5. Launch — Store submission, production Pages go-live, monitor usage
